WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:05.530
[Tommy]
There was no miracle

2
00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:07.570
involving my mother
other than her managing

3
00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:09.310
to die of old age.

4
00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:10.970
And he was too weak
to leave her.

5
00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:12.910
so I left all of them.

6
00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:18.080
[Rebecca]
What happened?

7
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.150
[Walt] One of your drivers
ran into a pickup

8
00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.550
parked on the easement.

9
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:22.720
I am sorry.

10
00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.190
I didn't ask for your dreams.

11
00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.120
You can't make my dreams
come true.

12
00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:27.360
Only I can do that.

13
00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:30.960
Your company invests
in drilling expeditions?

14
00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.730
We finance exploration. yes.

15
00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:35.360
Well. I need to drill
an existing well.

16
00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:37.170
It's a offshore rig

17
00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:39.030
that was damaged
in the hurricane.

18
00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:41.170
Your husband. he left you
quite a mess. didn't he?

19
00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:42.740
It wasn't intentional.

20
00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:44.170
but. yes. he did.

21
00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:45.670
[nurse]
Head up. There we go.

22
00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:47.510
How come I can't see?

23
00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.910
-Let me go get the doctor.
-Doctor! Doctor!

24
00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.350
[Angela]
Your father.

25
00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.380
He's rotting away
in some miserable excuse

26
00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:55.920
for a nursing home with nobody.

27
00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:57.350
[T.L.]
What are you doing here?

28
00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.190
We were thinking about
bringing you home.

29
00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:01.160
Let me go grab my things.

30
00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.090
[Tommy]
I already got them.

31
00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:06.100
* soft. gentle music

32
00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.990
[country music playing low
over radio]

33
00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:36.160
***

34
00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:39.800
-Tommy.
-Morning. Nate.

35
00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:43.500
Tommy. what is your father
doing on the porch?

36
00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.200
He's gonna stay with us a while.

37
00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:46.200
How long is a while?

38
00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:47.440
Till he dies.

39
00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.640
-Tommy.
-Don't get all worried about it.

40
00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.840
If he makes it a week
without me drowning him

41
00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:53.940
in that fucking swimming pool.
I'll be shocked.

42
00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:57.150
Tommy. you should really be
in Fort Worth. for one.

43
00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:59.110
Well. who's gonna do
what I do here?

44
00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:01.220
I mean. who's gonna fix
all the messes.

45
00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.020
manage the camp and the crews
and the contractors

46
00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.620
-and all that shit?
-I don't know.

47
00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:07.690
But you can't be a landman
and the president.

48
00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:08.860
Why not?

49
00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:09.790
There's lots of landmen
out there.

50
00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:10.790
Hire one.

51
00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:12.800
Then get him his own house.

52
00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:13.960
Morning. Nathan.

53
00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.230
Morning. baby.

54
00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:16.470
Hey. b-- Goddamn.

55
00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:18.070
You look like
a Mexican wrestler.

56
00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:19.100
Morning. Daddy.

57
00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:21.040
Hey. sweetie.

58
00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:24.470
Are y'all having
a little spa day or something?

59
00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:27.040
I want to glow for my birthday
party with the old folks.

60
00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:28.940
Your birthday's
in February. babe.

61
00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.480
They don't know that.

62
00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:32.850
They need little things
to look forward to and plan.

63
00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:34.120
You know. like little projects.

64
00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:35.520
-little chores.
-Oh.

65
00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:37.390
It's so cute. Daddy.

66
00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:39.620
They've been working so hard
decorating the party room.

67
00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:40.620
Oh?

68
00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:41.990
But we're not supposed to know.

69
00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.390
Big surprise.

70
00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:45.260
This nursing home
sounds like a really nice place.

71
00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:48.060
Could be somewhere
your father might like.

72
00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:50.670
Family stays at home. Nate.

73
00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.870
In fact. we're gonna throw

74
00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:54.670
a welcome dinner
for your dad tonight.

75
00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:55.940
Oh. good.

76
00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.610
What's the theme tonight. hon?

77
00:02:57.670 --> 00:02:59.480
Hold that thought.

78
00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:00.940
* soft. gentle music *

79
00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:02.710
T.L.. honey.

80
00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:04.450
If you were on death row

81
00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.680
and today was the day
of your execution.

82
00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:08.350
-what would your last meal be?
-What the fuck

83
00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:10.650
-kind of question is that?
-I'm just trying

84
00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:12.720
to get to the bottom
of your favorite meal.

85
00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:14.820
If I ask what's your favorite.

86
00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:16.190
you're gonna hem and haw
about it.

87
00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:18.860
"Maybe it's steak.
but I sure love pizza.

88
00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:21.260
-[chuckling]
-Maybe it's fajitas."

89
00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:23.830
But when I cut it down
to "You get one meal

90
00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:25.530
and then you're getting
electrocuted."

91
00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:27.940
people get real decisive.

92
00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:30.140
Best food I ever had in my life

93
00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:32.610
was at the marina
in Sabine Pass.

94
00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:35.140
-So. seafood. Mmm.
-Mmm.

95
00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:36.550
Barbecued blue crab.

96
00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:37.780
Crawfish boil.

97
00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:38.910
-Crabs.
-Mm-hmm.

98
00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:40.380
-Fried catfish.
-[chuckles]

99
00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:41.680
Oysters.

100
00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.720
[exhales sharply]
A man who knows what he wants.

101
00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.390
I like that.

102
00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.590
The theme tonight...

103
00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:52.700
...is pirates.
[chuckles softly]

104
00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:54.260
Isn't that cute. honey?

105
00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:56.370
You get to dress
like a little buccaneer.

106
00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:57.670
What's a buccaneer?

107
00:03:57.730 --> 00:03:59.400
Another name for "pirate."

108
00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:01.440
-Why do pirates need two names?
-That's a question

109
00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.510
for your history teacher. honey.

110
00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:05.310
Pirate's a general term. honey.

111
00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:07.680
Buccaneer is specific
to the Caribbean

112
00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.140
and the Gulf of Mexico.

113
00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:10.510
"Gulf of America" now. baby.

114
00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:11.910
I don't give a fuck
what they call it.

115
00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:13.880
You know. the salt water
out east of Galveston.

116
00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.350
[inhales sharply. groans]

117
00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:18.220
You all right. Nate?

118
00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:19.860
-Tachyarrhythmia.
-[Ainsley] Nate.

119
00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.390
-you speak another language?
-[Tommy chuckles]

120
00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:23.530
Matter of fact.
it does sound kind of like Dutch

121
00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:25.130
or Scandinavian
or something. honey.

122
00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:26.460
Just breathe. Nate.

123
00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.030
[Dale]
Morning. everybody.

124
00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:30.430
-Morning. Dale.
-[Ainsley] Morning.

125
00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:31.630
There ain't no more coffee?

126
00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:34.700
We didn't know if you
could have it on your diet.

127
00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:36.940
I'm not on a diet.

128
00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:39.270
Can you eat seafood. Dale?

129
00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:42.240
I ain't on a fucking diet.

130
00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:45.150
Oh. good. because the theme
tonight is pirates.

131
00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:46.820
So wear your best pirate outfit.

132
00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:48.320
[Dale]
Oh. great.

133
00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:49.890
Think I'll dress up
as a railroad commissioner.

134
00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:51.750
-[laughing]
-[Angela] Not trains.

135
00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:54.220
That's a different night. though
I got no idea the cuisine.

136
00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:55.820
Baby. we should look up
train food.

137
00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:57.330
What would train food be?

138
00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:58.460
-I don't know.
-Tommy. would you please

139
00:04:58.590 --> 00:04:59.930
pass these on to your son?

140
00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:01.230
What are they?

141
00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:02.900
Uh. drilling invoices.

142
00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:05.000
pipe suppliers. camp rentals.

143
00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:06.840
-Why did they send them here?
-I would love

144
00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:08.840
the answer to that question.
Tommy.

145
00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:12.610
Honey. we got to go.
We're gonna be late.

146
00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:13.780
Bye. honey.

147
00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:15.380
Bye. baby. I'll see you later.

148
00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:17.310
-Love you. Daddy. Mwah.
-Love you. Love you. sweetie.

149
00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:19.820
-Bye. Dale.
-[Dale] Bye. Have a good day.

150
00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:22.120
* soft. somber music *

151
00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:23.720
[door opens]

152
00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:26.150
[door closes]

153
00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:38.870
***

154
00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:50.410
Do you want some breakfast?

155
00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:00.360
Busy day?

156
00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:02.890
Every day's the same. Pop.

157
00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:04.990
Anyhow. just make yourself
at home.

158
00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:07.530
There's all kinds of shit
in the fridge.

159
00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:10.370
Who those horses belong to?

160
00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:12.470
Whichever old man
owns that field.

161
00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:16.410
Thinking the subdivision
stops with him.

162
00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:19.510
Stops with him for now.

163
00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:22.850
Till he dies and his kids
sell it off so fast

164
00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:25.550
it burns the grass
off the son of a bitch.

165
00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:29.550
Then we're staring at houses.

166
00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:32.350
I'll see you tonight.

167
00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:34.090
Yep.

168
00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:41.700
Supper around here
can be kind of an event.

169
00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:43.170
So I'm just warning you.

170
00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:45.200
An event?

171
00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:46.740
You just have to see it
to believe it.

172
00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:48.900
There ain't no fucking way
to describe it.

173
00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:54.510
* slow. gentle music *

174
00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:16.100
[dog barking in distance]

175
00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:25.510
***

176
00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:49.000
-[grunts softly]
-Hey.

177
00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:51.830
Hey back.

178
00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:56.040
What time
do you have to be at work?

179
00:07:58.140 --> 00:07:59.440
Don't.

180
00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.210
No particular time.

181
00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:03.480
Wells run just fine
on their own.

182
00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:07.520
Must be nice being rich.

183
00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:12.090
I haven't found
the downside yet.

184
00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:16.830
Course. I haven't gotten
a check yet either. so...

185
00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:19.600
really not much different
than yesterday at the moment.

186
00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:20.660
[chuckles]

187
00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:22.360
What will you do?

188
00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:24.170
I don't know.

189
00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:25.830
[inhales deeply]

190
00:08:25.930 --> 00:08:27.440
Maybe...

191
00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:30.710
buy a little place
we can visit on the weekends.

192
00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:33.610
Give Miguel a place
to run around.

193
00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:35.310
Someday...

194
00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:38.210
maybe have some more kids
that need to run around.

195
00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:48.360
If we're gonna do this.

196
00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:50.130
then let's do it.

197
00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:52.700
Both feet.

198
00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:56.030
I don't need a roommate.

199
00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:59.270
I'll do whatever you want.

200
00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:02.400
Okay then.

201
00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:11.050
What do you want?

202
00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:13.850
What do you think I want?

203
00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:17.050
Well. if I knew. I wouldn't
be asking the question.

204
00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:20.060
Well. I'm Catholic.

205
00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:23.730
Catholics don't exactly
shack up.

206
00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:31.600
You want to get married?

207
00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:36.340
-Do you want to get married?
-[chuckles]

208
00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:39.270
Why do women always answer
questions with questions?

209
00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:42.650
[scoffs] 'Cause we already know
what we think.

210
00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:45.380
I'm just trying to gauge
what you're thinking.

211
00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:50.250
I'd marry you tomorrow.

212
00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:51.820
Today.

213
00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:53.460
If a priest lived next door.

214
00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:55.220
I'd make him do it right now.

215
00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:57.530
There's a few more steps to it
than that.

216
00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:59.960
First. you have to ask me.

217
00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:04.330
And before you ask me.
you need to ask my father.

218
00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:07.370
I don't know your father.

219
00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:09.640
Well. then you have to meet him.

220
00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:12.440
Where's he live?

221
00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:14.710
Corpus.

222
00:10:14.810 --> 00:10:16.310
On the coast?

223
00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:18.680
He's a welder
for a Valero refinery.

224
00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:24.950
[grunts]
They know about me?

225
00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:26.490
I don't keep secrets.

226
00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:28.990
Well. can you give me
a sense of...

227
00:10:29.090 --> 00:10:31.890
their opinion on the subject?

228
00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:35.300
The opinion is mixed.

229
00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:38.270
[exhaling]

230
00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:39.770
[chuckles softly]

231
00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:42.140
I got to go talk
to my dad this morning.

232
00:10:42.270 --> 00:10:44.470
And then I'll head that way
after.

233
00:10:44.570 --> 00:10:46.140
Will you let 'em know
I'm coming?

234
00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:48.140
That's not how this works.

235
00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:49.850
-[scoffs]
-[chuckles]

236
00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:52.580
You want me.
figure it out and get me.

237
00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.690
-[chuckles softly]
-Hey.

238
00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:01.690
I don't believe in divorce.

239
00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:04.590
I believe in forever.

240
00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:08.260
I've only been with two men
in my life.

241
00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:11.300
and I'm not interested
in looking for a third.

242
00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:15.040
So. be sure.

243
00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:18.040
because this is gonna be
a lot of work.

244
00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:20.210
[grunts softly]

245
00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:23.980
Dating you hasn't exactly
been a picnic.

246
00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:25.250
Hey.

247
00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:29.650
-But it's got its perks.
-Mm.

248
00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:33.490
I'll call you
when I head that way.

249
00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:35.860
* soft. somber music *

250
00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:43.370
* gentle music *

251
00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:10.390
***

252
00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:38.750
***

253
00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:49.930
* "No Way Out"
by Jack Wharff Band playing *

254
00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:58.070
* No. it ain't right *

255
00:12:58.140 --> 00:12:59.410
* I finally said *

256
00:12:59.470 --> 00:13:00.940
* Rolled up with the devil *

257
00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:06.310
* Only way out
was in an early grave *

258
00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:08.480
* I walk the line *

259
00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:12.390
* Between the hard times
and barely living *

260
00:13:12.490 --> 00:13:14.560
* Whatever it takes *

261
00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:18.030
* Just to keep me sane *

262
00:13:18.890 --> 00:13:21.600
* But then again.
I kind of like the pain *

263
00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:24.630
* Wouldn't have it
any other way *

264
00:13:24.770 --> 00:13:29.300
* No way out.
nothing left to lose *

265
00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:32.140
* What you see is what you get *

266
00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:34.840
* 'Cause it ain't up to me... *

267
00:13:36.780 --> 00:13:38.450
-Did you order?
-[Cooper] Waitress is doing

268
00:13:38.550 --> 00:13:40.250
a pretty good job
of not noticing me.

269
00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:42.420
Well. that's 'cause you dress
like you run a Weedwacker

270
00:13:42.520 --> 00:13:44.290
on a landscaping crew.

271
00:13:44.350 --> 00:13:46.390
When you're hunting leases.
do you dress like that?

272
00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:48.020
Well. I ain't hunting leases
today.

273
00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:48.990
[chuckles]

274
00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:50.090
Morning. Tommy.

275
00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:51.160
Morning. honey.

276
00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:52.360
You in the middle or the end?

277
00:13:52.460 --> 00:13:53.830
My day just started.

278
00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:55.330
All right. well. I'm
gonna leave you the beer menu

279
00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:57.530
in case your day
started like mine.

280
00:13:57.630 --> 00:13:59.530
Since when did y'all get
a beer menu?

281
00:13:59.630 --> 00:14:01.170
Oil expo coming
to town next week.

282
00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:04.640
Those big-city boys
like their craft brews.

283
00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:06.370
Walking Stick Brewery.

284
00:14:06.470 --> 00:14:08.380
Spindletop Brewery.

285
00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:10.610
-Platipus?
-[chuckles]

286
00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:12.480
I don't know where
they come up with them names.

287
00:14:12.550 --> 00:14:14.450
They must've been drinking
when they made 'em up.

288
00:14:14.550 --> 00:14:16.220
Here's one just called "Eight."

289
00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:18.690
I think Troy Aikman owns that.

290
00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:20.520
-No shit.
-Mm-hmm.

291
00:14:20.620 --> 00:14:23.230
Might have to try that
just out of respect.

292
00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:24.360
Yeah. supposed to be healthy.

293
00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:25.960
A healthy beer?

294
00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:27.560
From your lips to God's ears.

295
00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:29.000
-Ellie.
-[Ellie chuckles]

296
00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:31.700
No. just bring me coffee
and four eggs over easy

297
00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:33.700
-and. uh. two sausage patties.
-You got it.

298
00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:34.770
How about you. darling?

299
00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:36.170
I'm fine.

300
00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:37.810
You sure about that?

301
00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:40.240
Looks like you could hula-hoop
through a Cheerio.

302
00:14:40.340 --> 00:14:41.710
I'm good. Thank you.

303
00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:44.080
All right. I'm gonna bring you
some biscuits anyway.

304
00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:48.780
Where you staying these days?

305
00:14:50.350 --> 00:14:51.920
With Ariana.

306
00:14:52.050 --> 00:14:54.290
Y'all figured it out?

307
00:14:56.990 --> 00:14:58.960
I'm gonna ask her to marry me.

308
00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:02.730
It's what she wants. Mm.

309
00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:04.030
I want it. too.

310
00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:05.230
She said that. did she?

311
00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:07.070
She did.

312
00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:08.840
Here you go.

313
00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:10.640
Thanks.

314
00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:19.010
There's some things
worth rushing.

315
00:15:19.110 --> 00:15:22.020
and others should move
caterpillar slow.

316
00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:24.550
Marriage is the latter. son.

317
00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:27.220
She's all I think about.

318
00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:29.660
When I close my eyes.
I still see her.

319
00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:32.030
Well. there's a little more
to it than that.

320
00:15:32.890 --> 00:15:34.230
Is there?

321
00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:36.460
You seem determined
to make your girl problem worse.

322
00:15:36.600 --> 00:15:38.770
so let's talk
about your other problem.

323
00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:40.040
Okay.

324
00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:43.270
I read over the contract.
and I don't see a problem.

325
00:15:43.410 --> 00:15:46.570
And you're still drilling
at six million per?

326
00:15:46.640 --> 00:15:48.140
And the six active wells?

327
00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:49.410
-Yeah.
-Yeah. you're gonna make

328
00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:51.110
five times that much.

329
00:15:51.210 --> 00:15:52.650
but not this month.

330
00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:54.120
Not this year.

331
00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:56.250
Sonrisa's covering
drilling costs. so it's fine.

332
00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:58.490
Oh. so. they put $40 million
dollars in a checking account

333
00:15:58.590 --> 00:16:00.120
and you didn't tell me about it?

334
00:16:00.220 --> 00:16:01.290
I thought that...

335
00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:02.960
No. they just-- They pay.

336
00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:04.730
The loan's to you

337
00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:07.460
with a meter running
and a fifty-fifty split.

338
00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:09.930
Thirty days to build
a pad and drill.

339
00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:12.570
30 more days to fill the tanks.

340
00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:14.840
and you don't get paid
till the 27th of the next month.

341
00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:16.870
So who the fuck's
paying your bills?

342
00:16:16.970 --> 00:16:17.840
I thought the loan paid it.

343
00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:19.610
What loan?

344
00:16:19.710 --> 00:16:21.240
Where is it?

345
00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:24.780
Did you open an LLC
and a bank account for the LLC?

346
00:16:24.880 --> 00:16:27.180
Is this loan company
stroking you a check

347
00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:30.320
for $40 million dollars
to put in the bank?

348
00:16:30.450 --> 00:16:34.860
Did you hire an accounting firm
to service debt and payables?

349
00:16:43.530 --> 00:16:44.730
[closes cigarette case]

350
00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:51.740
How the fuck did you talk
these crews into drilling?

351
00:16:53.380 --> 00:16:57.510
I showed 'em the approval
letter and the agreement.

352
00:16:57.650 --> 00:16:59.250
-Told 'em who I was and...
-Okay.

353
00:16:59.350 --> 00:17:01.320
Now we're getting somewhere.

354
00:17:05.890 --> 00:17:08.220
-Thank you. honey.
-Here you go. babe.

355
00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:11.830
That explains the $44 million
dollars' worth of invoices

356
00:17:11.930 --> 00:17:13.400
that we got.

357
00:17:19.630 --> 00:17:21.240
You don't know
how this business works.

358
00:17:21.340 --> 00:17:23.240
You think you do. but you don't.

359
00:17:23.370 --> 00:17:26.610
And you damn sure don't know
who you got in business with.

360
00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:29.640
But since you're so terrible
at it.

361
00:17:29.710 --> 00:17:31.310
it might save you.

362
00:17:32.910 --> 00:17:35.120
M-TEX is gonna buy your leases.

363
00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:38.720
And we'll cancel the note
and cover your costs.

364
00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:42.290
The drilling expenses
and the surface lease.

365
00:17:43.060 --> 00:17:44.560
Maintenance. The whole thing.

366
00:17:44.690 --> 00:17:45.890
So I get nothing?

367
00:17:45.990 --> 00:17:47.700
You have nothing.

368
00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:50.030
No. I take that back.
You-you found a blind spot.

369
00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:51.530
You got good instincts.

370
00:17:51.600 --> 00:17:53.070
And shock of all shocks.

371
00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:55.070
apparently. you're
a hell of a salesman.

372
00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:56.400
So I'm gonna hire you back.

373
00:17:56.540 --> 00:17:57.740
and I'm gonna start
to teach you--

374
00:17:57.840 --> 00:17:59.170
I ain't working no crew.

375
00:17:59.270 --> 00:18:00.840
No. you're running one.

376
00:18:00.940 --> 00:18:03.610
And you're gonna do
exactly what I tell you to do.

377
00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:08.780
Three thousand barrels a day

378
00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:10.250
and I don't see a dime of it?

379
00:18:10.350 --> 00:18:12.690
You were never gonna see
a fucking dime.

380
00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:16.360
They would foreclose
on your leases

381
00:18:16.420 --> 00:18:20.700
and flip 'em and leave you
in a mountain of fucking debt

382
00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:24.300
and a ruined name in the basin.

383
00:18:24.400 --> 00:18:26.930
A landman makes $9.000 a month.

384
00:18:27.030 --> 00:18:28.270
plus bonus.

385
00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:30.410
Now. when I show you
how this deal works.

386
00:18:30.510 --> 00:18:31.640
with your instincts--

387
00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:33.280
and I never had 'em.
not like you do--

388
00:18:33.410 --> 00:18:35.880
you make $9.000 a minute.

389
00:18:35.980 --> 00:18:38.780
But you got to know the rules
of the game to bend 'em.

390
00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:41.420
And you really got
to know 'em to break 'em.

391
00:18:43.590 --> 00:18:45.490
-I got to sign something?
-Shit yeah.

392
00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:46.720
About 300 pages.

393
00:18:46.820 --> 00:18:49.120
once Nate writes it up.

394
00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:50.960
All right. When do I start?

395
00:18:51.090 --> 00:18:52.960
Well. you're with me now.

396
00:18:53.090 --> 00:18:54.660
When do you want to start?

397
00:18:55.460 --> 00:18:57.500
I got to drive to Corpus. so...

398
00:18:58.430 --> 00:18:59.970
...when I get back?

399
00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:02.140
What's in Corpus?

400
00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:04.710
Ariana's parents.

401
00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:08.580
Goddamn.

402
00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:10.650
Dad.

403
00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:14.550
I love her.

404
00:19:15.580 --> 00:19:18.390
If it were only that simple.

405
00:19:20.690 --> 00:19:22.260
And you do need
to eat something.

406
00:19:22.320 --> 00:19:23.660
"Hula-hooping through a Cheerio"

407
00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:25.360
-ain't a fucking compliment.
-[phone buzzing]

408
00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:29.160
Hey. Nate.

409
00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:31.800
Blanton's attorneys
have a proposal.

410
00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:33.000
Well. I'm headed that way.

411
00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:34.000
No time.

412
00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:35.500
They want to meet in an hour.

413
00:19:35.640 --> 00:19:37.770
After that. we lose 'em to trial
with the clock ticking.

414
00:19:37.840 --> 00:19:39.340
All right.
Well. go to Fort Worth.

415
00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:41.480
but don't agree to anything
till you run it by me.

416
00:19:41.540 --> 00:19:42.880
Rebecca was supposed

417
00:19:42.980 --> 00:19:44.710
to meet with the sheriff
at the incident site.

418
00:19:44.810 --> 00:19:46.210
What incident site?

419
00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:47.180
We had a vehicle accident

420
00:19:47.320 --> 00:19:49.680
at one of our lease roads.

421
00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:52.090
You finish my breakfast.

422
00:19:52.190 --> 00:19:55.060
-I guess I don't get any today.
-All right.

423
00:19:59.790 --> 00:20:01.130
How bad?

424
00:20:01.230 --> 00:20:02.500
They don't get worse.

425
00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:04.970
And I'm just hearing
about this shit now?

426
00:20:05.070 --> 00:20:06.500
You had the funeral.

427
00:20:06.570 --> 00:20:09.070
and we don't have enough
information yet to present it.

428
00:20:09.170 --> 00:20:11.170
-Nate. goddamn it.
-Tommy.

429
00:20:11.270 --> 00:20:12.570
you're the president now.

430
00:20:12.710 --> 00:20:14.880
-This issue isn't even--
-I'm also the president.

431
00:20:15.010 --> 00:20:17.550
I still run operations.
and I can't do it

432
00:20:17.680 --> 00:20:19.050
if I don't know everything.

433
00:20:19.180 --> 00:20:20.380
Sorry. Tommy.

434
00:20:20.480 --> 00:20:21.480
We never told Monty
about these things

435
00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:22.720
until they were fleshed out.

436
00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:23.820
Monty didn't run the basin.

437
00:20:23.920 --> 00:20:25.320
Monty ran Fort Worth.

438
00:20:25.390 --> 00:20:27.960
I ran the basin.
and I still run it.

439
00:20:29.690 --> 00:20:30.930
Understood.

440
00:20:31.030 --> 00:20:32.590
Send me a pin to this crash.

441
00:20:32.730 --> 00:20:34.930
* low. tense music *

442
00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:43.940
[tires screeching]

443
00:21:02.520 --> 00:21:03.590
[shuts off engine]

444
00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:06.030
***

445
00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:09.300
Why didn't you call me?

446
00:21:09.400 --> 00:21:10.930
I called your lawyer.

447
00:21:11.030 --> 00:21:12.330
You're the big man now.

448
00:21:12.430 --> 00:21:13.600
Lawyer ain't the first call.

449
00:21:13.740 --> 00:21:14.970
Lawyer's the last call.

450
00:21:15.070 --> 00:21:16.240
And that's my call.

451
00:21:16.340 --> 00:21:18.710
Who pissed in your Froot Loops?

452
00:21:18.810 --> 00:21:19.940
God.

453
00:21:20.040 --> 00:21:21.140
It's the first thing
he did this morning.

454
00:21:21.240 --> 00:21:22.940
Now walk me through this shit.

455
00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:26.310
Sand hauler blasting down this
road well over the speed limit.

456
00:21:26.450 --> 00:21:27.750
How do you know that?

457
00:21:27.820 --> 00:21:30.750
Well. he was traveling
at an unsafe speed.

458
00:21:30.850 --> 00:21:32.220
How do you know it was unsafe?

459
00:21:32.290 --> 00:21:35.060
Judging by that mangled pickup
that got tossed

460
00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:36.760
into that pumpjack...

461
00:21:37.730 --> 00:21:39.260
...it was unsafe.

462
00:21:39.330 --> 00:21:41.900
He didn't have time
to brake or evade.

463
00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:43.900
[Tommy] Is this
the pickup driver's property?

464
00:21:43.970 --> 00:21:45.100
[Walt]
It is not.

465
00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:46.830
-[Tommy] Whose is it?
-Yours.

466
00:21:46.930 --> 00:21:48.940
And the son of a bitch didn't
have permission to use it.

467
00:21:49.040 --> 00:21:52.040
[Walt] Tommy. you ain't got
to argue this with me.

468
00:21:52.140 --> 00:21:53.510
[Tommy]
Oh. I disagree.

469
00:21:53.640 --> 00:21:55.540
Your police report's
gonna be the basis

470
00:21:55.640 --> 00:21:56.980
for their fucking lawsuit.

471
00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:59.750
You start using words
like "unsafe speeds"

472
00:21:59.810 --> 00:22:01.150
and shit like that.

473
00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:03.220
well. that alters
the opinion of the attorneys

474
00:22:03.320 --> 00:22:05.090
and the court
and a potential jury.

475
00:22:05.190 --> 00:22:09.190
The son of a bitch was going 60
down a caliche road at midnight.

476
00:22:09.290 --> 00:22:11.590
[Tommy]
It's my fucking road. Walt.

477
00:22:11.660 --> 00:22:13.560
I'll put up
"65 mile-an-hour" signs

478
00:22:13.660 --> 00:22:16.360
all over this son of a bitch
this afternoon.

479
00:22:16.500 --> 00:22:18.870
Well. that ain't the worst idea
you ever had.

480
00:22:18.970 --> 00:22:20.870
Yeah. well.
I'm just getting started.

481
00:22:21.670 --> 00:22:22.900
Now. what's this rig?

482
00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:24.940
[Walt] That's what I was telling
your lawyer.

483
00:22:25.010 --> 00:22:27.680
He ran that hose
in the back window of his truck.

484
00:22:27.780 --> 00:22:30.650
Been sucking exhaust fumes
for who knows how long.

485
00:22:30.750 --> 00:22:31.980
You doing an autopsy?

486
00:22:32.050 --> 00:22:33.880
I ordered one.

487
00:22:41.320 --> 00:22:43.020
Mike. this is Tommy.

488
00:22:43.160 --> 00:22:46.390
Is your investigator on the way
out here to this accident site?

489
00:22:47.530 --> 00:22:49.360
No. the other one.

490
00:22:50.200 --> 00:22:51.870
No. the vehicle accident.

491
00:22:53.600 --> 00:22:55.040
No. the sand hauler.

492
00:22:55.140 --> 00:22:57.810
How many damn claims
have we submitted. Mike?

493
00:22:57.910 --> 00:23:00.710
He don't even know which
accident you're talking about.

494
00:23:00.840 --> 00:23:02.480
Well. get him out here.

495
00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:04.250
No. today.

496
00:23:04.350 --> 00:23:05.910
We're not the defendant
in this one.

497
00:23:06.050 --> 00:23:07.580
We're the plaintiff.

498
00:23:07.720 --> 00:23:10.620
If you send somebody out here
to photograph this evidence.

499
00:23:11.490 --> 00:23:12.950
Uh...

500
00:23:14.560 --> 00:23:15.660
[exhales]

501
00:23:16.420 --> 00:23:17.730
Walt. if you want something
done right.

502
00:23:17.830 --> 00:23:19.860
you got to do it
your fucking self.

503
00:23:23.570 --> 00:23:25.530
-We photographed the scene.
-[phone clicking]

504
00:23:25.630 --> 00:23:26.870
Well. no offense. Walt.

505
00:23:26.930 --> 00:23:28.840
but getting evidence
from a government agency

506
00:23:28.940 --> 00:23:32.440
is about as speedy a process
as getting a tattoo removed.

507
00:23:33.480 --> 00:23:36.110
So call you from now on.

508
00:23:36.210 --> 00:23:37.650
Nate said call the lawyer.

509
00:23:37.750 --> 00:23:40.750
No. you call me and only me.

510
00:23:40.850 --> 00:23:42.120
I prefer it.

511
00:23:43.050 --> 00:23:44.850
That lawyer's
wound pretty tight.

512
00:23:44.950 --> 00:23:46.850
If she swallowed a lump of coal.

513
00:23:46.950 --> 00:23:49.420
she'd make a diamond
in three days.

514
00:23:49.490 --> 00:23:51.730
* low. somber music *

515
00:24:05.140 --> 00:24:07.340
[phone ringing]

516
00:24:09.110 --> 00:24:10.210
Hey. What do you know. Tommy?

517
00:24:10.310 --> 00:24:12.950
Evidently.
I don't know shit. Dale.

518
00:24:13.010 --> 00:24:14.750
What happened out
at that cleanup?

519
00:24:14.820 --> 00:24:17.350
We walked into a cloud of H2S.

520
00:24:17.450 --> 00:24:18.820
Nate didn't fucking tell you?

521
00:24:18.920 --> 00:24:20.720
Nobody told me. bud.

522
00:24:21.820 --> 00:24:23.930
Oh. shit. I'm sorry. Tommy.

523
00:24:24.030 --> 00:24:24.930
Uh...

524
00:24:25.030 --> 00:24:26.260
Yeah.

525
00:24:26.360 --> 00:24:28.200
Uh. it was a bad deal.

